ADAPTIVE QUIZ SYSTEM — JAVA SWING FRONTEND

Included files:
- DBConnection.java: Oracle JDBC connection settings.
- AdaptiveQuizApp.java: Swing UI with student registration, question management,
  adaptive quiz, result display, and quiz history.

REQUIREMENTS
- JDK 8 or newer (JDK 11/17/21 recommended)
- Oracle Database with the six tables created from the supplied SQL scripts
- Oracle JDBC driver (ojdbc8/ojdbc11, appropriate for your JDK)

SETUP
1. Create a Java project in your IDE.
2. Add DBConnection.java and AdaptiveQuizApp.java to the same source folder.
3. Add the Oracle JDBC driver JAR to the project's libraries/build path.
4. Open DBConnection.java and set:
   URL, USERNAME, PASSWORD
   Example URL: jdbc:oracle:thin:@localhost:1521/XEPDB1
   Your Oracle service name may be different.
5. Ensure the six tables exist:
   Student, Subject, Question, Quiz_Attempt, Student_Response, Quiz_Result
6. Run AdaptiveQuizApp.java.

FEATURES
- Register and search students
- Add questions with four options and difficulty
- Take a quiz, starting at Easy
- Correct answers raise difficulty; wrong answers lower it
- Save every answer and final result in Oracle
- View quiz history

NOTES
- The app expects the table and column names from the supplied Oracle SQL scripts.
- For the first test, insert subjects and sample questions with the SQL scripts.
- It is a student project starter; add role-based admin login, edit/delete screens,
  stronger validation, and more questions as needed.
- The quiz ends when the chosen question count is reached or no unused questions
  remain for the selected subject.
